msgid "Usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/meow_readme.md:64
msgid "API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/meow_readme.md:66
msgid "meow(options, [minimistOptions])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/meow_readme.md:68
msgid "Returns an object with:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/meow_readme.md:70
msgid "`input` *(array)* - Non-flag arguments"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/meow_readme.md:71
msgid "`flags` *(object)* - Flags converted to camelCase"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/meow_readme.md:72
msgid "`pkg` *(object)* - The `package.json` object"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/meow_readme.md:73
msgid "`help` *(object)* - The help text used with `--help`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/meow_readme.md:74
msgid ""
"`showHelp([code=0])` *(function)* - Show the help text and exit with "
"`code`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/meow_readme.md:76
msgid "options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/meow_readme.md:78
msgid "Type: `object`, `array`, `string`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/meow_readme.md:80
msgid "Can either be a string/array that is the `help` or an options object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/meow_readme.md:82
msgid "description"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/meow_readme.md:84
msgid ""
"Type: `string`, `boolean` Default: The package.json `\"description\"` "
"property"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/meow_readme.md:87
msgid "A description to show above the help text."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/meow_readme.md:89 ../../source/meow_readme.md:104
#: ../../source/meow_readme.md:113
msgid "Set it to `false` to disable it altogether."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/meow_readme.md:91
msgid "help"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/meow_readme.md:93
msgid "Type: `string`, `boolean`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/meow_readme.md:95
msgid "The help text you want shown."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/meow_readme.md:97
msgid ""
"The input is reindented and starting/ending newlines are trimmed which "
"means you can use a [template "
"literal](https://developer.mozilla.org/en/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/template_strings)"
" without having to care about using the correct amount of indent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/meow_readme.md:99
msgid ""
"<del>If it's an array each item will be a line.</del>   *(Still "
"supported, but you should use a template literal instead.)*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/meow_readme.md:102
msgid "The description will be shown above your help text automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/meow_readme.md:106
msgid "version"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/meow_readme.md:108
msgid ""
"Type: `string`, `boolean`   Default: The package.json `\"version\"` "
"property"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/meow_readme.md:111
msgid "Set a custom version output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/meow_readme.md:115
msgid "pkg"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/meow_readme.md:117
msgid "Type: `string`, `object`   Default: Closest package.json upwards"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/meow_readme.md:120
msgid "Relative path to package.json or as an object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/meow_readme.md:122
msgid "argv"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/meow_readme.md:124
msgid "Type: `array`   Default: `process.argv.slice(2)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/meow_readme.md:127
msgid "Custom arguments object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/meow_readme.md:129
msgid "minimistOptions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/meow_readme.md:131
#, python-brace-format
msgid "Type: `object`   Default: `{}`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/meow_readme.md:134
msgid ""
"Minimist [options](https://github.com/substack/minimist#var-argv"
"--parseargsargs-opts)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/meow_readme.md:136
msgid ""
"Keys passed to the minimist `default` option are "
"[decamelized](https://github.com/sindresorhus/decamelize), so you can for"
" example pass in `fooBar: 'baz'` and have it be the default for the "
"`--foo-bar` flag."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/meow_readme.md:139
msgid "Promises"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/meow_readme.md:141
msgid ""
"Meow will make unhandled rejected promises [fail "
"loudly](https://github.com/sindresorhus/loud-rejection) instead of the "
"default silent fail. Meaning you don't have to manually `.catch()` "
"promises used in your CLI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/meow_readme.md:144
msgid "Tips"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/meow_readme.md:146
msgid ""
"See [`chalk`](https://github.com/chalk/chalk) if you want to colorize the"
" terminal output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/meow_readme.md:148
msgid ""
"See [`get-stdin`](https://github.com/sindresorhus/get-stdin) if you want "
"to accept input from stdin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/meow_readme.md:150
msgid ""
"See [`update-notifier`](https://github.com/yeoman/update-notifier) if you"
" want update notifications."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/meow_readme.md:152
msgid ""
"See [`configstore`](https://github.com/yeoman/configstore) if you need to"
" persist some data."
msgstr ""

